---
/**
 * §13 · AFFILIATIONS & PARTNERS — audit 1.13
 *
 * Audit 1.13, verbatim: "Before the footer, include a section showcasing the
 * school's academic and institutional affiliations/partners through neatly
 * displayed logos." Audit 1.14 then places Achievements after it, so the two
 * run in that order in index.astro.
 *
 * ⚠ A RAIL, NOT A SIX-UP GRID. The set grew from six marks to seventeen. A grid
 * would have run to three rows and turned a quiet credential band into the
 * loudest block on the page; the rail keeps it one row tall at every width and
 * takes any number of logos without another layout decision. It is the same
 * AsRailSlider every other rail in this project uses — a native scroller with
 * NO AUTOPLAY, so nothing moves unless the reader moves it.
 *
 * ═══ CAPTIONS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * ⚠ THIRTEEN OF THE SEVENTEEN NOTES ARE VERIFIED from the school's own record
 * as already transcribed in this project:
 *   NPSC · AFS · FICCI    — PhilosophyStory: "Memberships: NPSC, AFS, FICCI."
 *   Microsoft (both)      — MethodologyPage: "100 Microsoft Innovative Educator
 *                           Experts → a Microsoft Showcase School."
 *   Inspire Award MANAK   — OlympiadPage: "Student innovations selected for the
 *                           Department of Science & Technology's MANAK scheme."
 *   Vidyarthi Vigyan M.   — OlympiadPage: "qualified to the NATIONAL level."
 *   NCSC                  — OlympiadPage: "National-level qualification."
 *   CBSE · Sunbeam group · EducationWorld · Brainfeed · NCC — as before.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ FOUR ARE NOT VERIFIED — Hindustan Olympiad, Behes, School Cinema and
 * UMEED appear nowhere in the school's published record as transcribed here.
 * The client supplied the marks for this section, so the relationship is their
 * assertion, not this project's. What that means for the captions: the two that
 * carry a note carry the tagline PRINTED ON THE MARK ITSELF ("Debate for All",
 * "A Positive Living Initiative") — transcription, not a claim — and the other
 * two print no note at all rather than have one invented for them. If the
 * school can say what each relationship is, the notes go in and this paragraph
 * comes out.
 *
 * ⚠ education-world.png IS RETIRED. The old file was a generic stock
 * "EDUCATION · GLOBAL ACADEMIC" graduation-cap graphic captioned as Education
 * World's identity, which it was not — logged as asset request B1. The client
 * has now supplied the real EducationWorld mark, so B1 is closed. The stock
 * file is left on disk but no longer imported.
 *
 * ═══ WHY THE IMPORTS POINT AT logos/trimmed/ ═════════════════════════
 * Every mark is fitted into one box with object-fit: contain, so how big a
 * logo LOOKS is decided by how much of its own file the mark occupies — and the
 * supplied files disagreed wildly. CBSE, NCC and Brainfeed fill their canvas
 * edge to edge; AFS used 30% of its 500x500, Hindustan Olympiad 31%, FICCI 43%,
 * EducationWorld 48%. In identical boxes the first group rendered at twice the
 * size of the second and the row read as broken rather than as a set.
 *
 * scripts/logo-trim.mjs crops each file to its mark’s true bounding box and
 * re-pads by a uniform 3%, so all of them now use the same share of their
 * canvas. It recolours and rescales nothing — the mark’s own pixels come
 * through untouched — and it writes to logos/trimmed/, leaving the client’s
 * originals in logos/ exactly as delivered. Add a logo, re-run the script.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { getSchool, getAffiliations } from '../../lib/cms';
import CmsImage from '../ui/CmsImage.astro';
import AccentHeading from '../ui/AccentHeading.astro';
import AsRailSlider from "../academics/assessment/AsRailSlider.astro";
import rocket from "../../assets/icons/rocketpaper.png";
import wave from "../../assets/icons/wave.png";


const school = await getSchool();
const { heading, partners } = await getAffiliations();

---

<section class="affil" aria-labelledby="ach-heading">
  {
    /* Decorative. Sits in the section's own top padding, clear of the heading —
      verified by box overlap, not by eye. */
  }
  <Image
    class="affil__rocket"
    src={rocket}
    alt=""
    aria-hidden="true"
    widths={[200, 400]}
    sizes="200px"
    loading="lazy"
  />

  <div class="u-container">
    <div class="affil__head" data-reveal>
      <AccentHeading class="ach__heading t-h2-sans" id="ach-heading" split text={heading} />
    </div>

    {/* ⚠ NO `bleed`. The section is `overflow: hidden` for the drifting rocket,
        so a track that bled into the container padding would be clipped at the
        edge rather than run under it. */}
    <AsRailSlider
      label="Affiliations and recognition partners"
      id="affil-rail"
      total={partners.length}
      per={6}
      perMd={3}
      perSm={2}
      class="affil__rail"
    >
      {
        partners.map((p) => (
          <li class="affil__item">
            <span class="affil__mark">
              {/* widths/sizes must exceed the rendered box. With `width: auto`
                the layout width follows the INTRINSIC width of whichever
                candidate the browser picks, so `sizes="120px"` silently pinned
                every mark to 120px wide and the CSS caps never bound. */}
              {/* ⚠ EAGER, NOT LAZY, AND fetchpriority="low" INSTEAD. Native lazy
                  loading measures against the VIEWPORT, and a tile scrolled off
                  to the right of the rail is outside it — so pressing the arrow
                  showed an empty white tile that filled in a beat later. These
                  are 180px marks; fetching all seventeen costs little, and low
                  priority keeps them from competing with the hero. */}
              <CmsImage
                file={p.logo}
                alt={`${p.name} logo`}
                sizes="180px"
                fallbackWidth={420}
                loading="eager"
                decoding="async"
                fetchpriority="low"
              />
            </span>
            {p.note && <span class="affil__note">{p.note}</span>}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </AsRailSlider>

    <p class="affil__legal t-tabular">
      CBSE Affiliation No. {school.affiliationNo} · School Code {
        school.schoolCode
      }
    </p>
  </div>
  <Image
    class="affil__wave"
    src={wave}
    alt=""
    aria-hidden="true"
    widths={[100, 200]}
    sizes="100px"
    loading="lazy"
  />
</section>

<style>
  .affil {
    position: relative;

    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--sb-sand);
    padding-block: var(--sb-section-y);
  }

  .affil__rocket {
    position: absolute;
    top: 16px;
    right: 150px;
    width: 100px;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.8;

    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    animation: affil-drift 7s ease-in-out infinite;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .affil__wave {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 50px;
    left: 100px;
    width: 22px;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.8;

    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    user-select: none;
    animation: affil-drift 7s ease-in-out infinite;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  @keyframes affil-drift {
    0%,
    100% {
      transform: translateY(0) rotate(0deg);
    }
    50% {
      transform: translateY(-14px) rotate(-3deg);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .affil__rocket {
      animation: none;
    }
  }

  .affil > .u-container {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .affil__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--sb-8);
  }

  .affil__heading {
    font-family: var(--sb-font-sans);
    font-size: var(--sb-caption);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sb-text-muted);
  }

  /* ⚠ THE RAIL'S HEAD SLOT IS EMPTY HERE, so the arrows and counter would sit
     alone on a full-width row. Pulling that row up against the centred heading
     keeps the band as short as it was as a grid. */
  /* ⚠⚠ ANCHORED ON .affil, NOT ON .affil__rail. Astro stamps its scope
     attribute at BUILD time onto elements in THIS component’s template — and
     .affil__rail is not one of them, it is a class handed to AsRailSlider and
     printed by that component, so it carries no data-astro-cid of ours. Both
     rules below silently did nothing until they hung off .affil, which is in
     this template and does carry it. */
  .affil :global(.sl-rail__head) {
    margin-top: calc(var(--sb-6) * -1);
  }

  /* ⚠⚠ THE TRACK IS A SCROLL CONTAINER, and `overflow-x: auto` clips the Y axis
     too — there is no such thing as scrolling one axis and letting the other
     spill. So the tile’s 8px hover lift and its drop shadow were being sheared
     off against the counter row above. The room has to come from padding INSIDE
     the scrollport; a margin on the tile would only move the clip line. */
  .affil :global(.sl-rail__track) {
    padding-block: 16px 20px;
  }

  /* Deliberately quiet — a low-volume band between two loud sections.
     Loud partner logos read as advertising rather than credentials. */
  .affil__item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    /* flex-start, not center: one caption runs to two lines, and centring the
       whole stack lifted that tile's mark 9px above the other five. Anchoring
       the top keeps every mark and every caption on one line regardless of how
       long a caption is. */
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: var(--sb-6);
    min-height: 226px;
    padding: var(--sb-7) var(--sb-5);
    text-align: center;
    border: var(--sb-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-2);
    background: #fff;
    transition:
      border-color var(--sb-dur-link) ease,
      transform var(--sb-dur-image) var(--sb-ease),
      box-shadow var(--sb-dur-image) var(--sb-ease),
      background-color var(--sb-dur-link) ease;
  }

  /* The tile lifts, warms and deepens; the mark inside grows a little more than
     the tile does, so the logo reads as coming forward rather than the whole
     card simply sliding. */
  .affil__item:hover {
    border-color: var(--sb-violet);
    transform: translateY(-8px);
    box-shadow: var(--sb-shadow-card-hover);
    background: var(--sb-violet-wash);
  }

  .affil__item:hover .affil__mark :global(img) {
    transform: scale(1.09);
  }
  .affil__item:hover .affil__note {
    color: var(--sb-violet-dark);
  }

  /* FIXED-HEIGHT BOX, and that is the whole trick. The marks run from 157×196
     (a tall Microsoft shield) to 380×299 (a wide CBSE emblem); letting each one
     size itself leaves every caption at a different height and the row reads as
     ragged. The box is a fixed size and `object-fit: contain` fits each mark
     inside it, so all of them share a height and every caption starts on one
     line.

     Sizing the BOX rather than the image is also what makes this deterministic:
     max-width/max-height on the image itself deferred to whichever srcset
     candidate the browser chose. */
  .affil__mark {
    width: 100%;
    height: 118px;
  }

  .affil__mark :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    transition: transform var(--sb-dur-image) var(--sb-ease);
  }

  .affil__note {
    font-size: var(--sb-caption);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--sb-text-muted);
    transition: color var(--sb-dur-link) ease;
  }

  .affil__legal {
    margin: var(--sb-7) 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--sb-caption);
    color: var(--sb-text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    /* The band is short here and the plane would sit directly behind the
       heading. Smaller, and held up in the top padding. */
    .affil__rocket {
      width: 104px;
      top: -4px;
      right: -12px;
      opacity: 0.7;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 479px) {
    .affil__item {
      min-height: 168px;
      gap: var(--sb-5);
      padding: var(--sb-6) var(--sb-4);
    }
    /* Only the box changes — the image fills it, so no image override needed. */
    .affil__mark {
      height: 86px;
    }
  }
</style>
